## 211. Important Note About Ambiguous Questions

Some classification questions can accidentally have more than one valid rule.

For example:

```text
2, 3, 5, 9
```

Possible properties can be invented endlessly.

Therefore, exam-quality classification requires:

```text
\boxed{\text{One strong, natural, syllabus-relevant rule}}
```

Do not accept a weak or artificially constructed pattern merely because it technically works.

