## 213. Ultimate Exam Rule

> **Do not ask "Which one looks different?"**
>
> Ask:
>
> **"What exact property groups the maximum number of items together, and which item fails that property?"**

That single question solves a large percentage of classification problems.

---

## 214. One-Line Formula

```text
\boxed{\text{Classification}=\text{Common Property}+\text{Outlier Detection}}
```

Or:

```text
Find GROUP
    ↓
Find PROPERTY
    ↓
Find EXCEPTION
    ↓
ANSWER
```

